    "created_at": "2019-02-26T15:24:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-03-01T14:31:48Z",
    "body": "Isn't the behavior of how to handle deferred content under certain circumstances in the intereset of web API implementors? \r\n\r\nSimilarly to how one may expect deferred images to load in for printing, lazily loaded content should preferrably load in to be cached for offline experiences (e.g. user presses \"Add to home screen\"). This is what Chromium intends to do: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=905432",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/467481515/reactions",
